sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task (driver workflow), ADR 0239 orbit.dependencies.v1, Recall swamp-owns-dependencies + deps-one-group-per-project, R1-R3.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 3, 9, 14, 15, 18 (no input read, no attempt records, head check folded into the read, no report or fail step).
  %% Decided: Nick 2026-11-02, project:maintenance:detect becomes project:maintenance:inspect: per-Project opt-in, default branch only, blob-SHA short-circuit, changed files read through the GitHub App with no clone, daily registry and advisory check, no begin or finish notes, no orbit-gateway calls. The kind keeps its name until the code follows.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: project:maintenance:inspect
  %% kind: project.detect
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  %% lane REG icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>tree · blobs
  participant REG as Registries<br/>Packagist · npm
  CLI->>GW: maintenance:inspect 4<br/>--open
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit project:maintenance:inspect 4 --open`
  %%> - syntax: `project:maintenance:inspect <project> [--open] [--idempotency-key=KEY]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Project
  %%> - `--open`: open the update task group for the findings; without it, inspect shows the findings and creates nothing
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  %%> - the hourly `maintenance-projects` Schedule admits the same kind with `--open`, for each opted-in Project
  Note over GW: Validate, mint read token<br/>task #5150 · vault key
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Gateway
  %%> - maintenance is on for Project 4 (`project:maintenance:enable`); it is off by default, so customer repositories stay untouched
  %%> - Project 4 reads its repository through the GitHub App and has a default branch; only that branch is inspected
  %%> - no other `project.detect`, `project.routine` or `project.observe` task runs for Project 4
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - mints a GitHub App token with `contents: read` for this repository only
  %%> - puts it in the `orbit-control-inputs` vault as `project-dependency-read-5150` (R3)
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5150 recorded with the full intent; no Node is a target
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>project-maintenance-inspect
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the repository and its default branch
  %%> - the blob SHAs of the last inspection and the stored package list
  %%> - whether the registry check is due: once a day, or at once with `--open`
  %%> - the vault key name of the token, never the token
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5150
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the caller follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>GH: Read the manifest SHAs<br/>Git tree · one request
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the default branch head and its tree through the GitHub App, with the token from `vault.get`
  %%> - picks the blob SHAs of `composer.json`, `composer.lock`, `package.json`, workspace `package.json` files and the JavaScript lockfile of each policy path
  %%> Short-circuit:
  %%> - SHAs equal to the last inspection: the next step is skipped by its `guard`
  %%> Why no clone:
  %%> - one tree request per opted-in Project each hour is cheap; a clone is not
  opt a manifest SHA changed
    SW->>GH: Read the changed files<br/>blobs by SHA · no clone
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads again only the sources whose SHAs changed, by blob SHA, so they match the tree just read; other sources keep their stored packages
    %%> - lists the installed packages and their versions from the lockfiles
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the new package list, in the step's output
  end
  opt check due or a package list changed
    SW->>REG: Check latest, advisories<br/>Packagist · npm · advisory DB
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - compares the package list with the latest Packagist and npm versions and with the advisory database
    %%> Cache:
    %%> - answers are cached per package across Projects, so a package that many Projects use is asked once a day
    %%> Why daily:
    %%> - new releases and advisories appear without any change in the repository
  end
  Note over SW: Find the updates<br/>policy · one package group
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - applies release-age policy, version constraints and the Project's exceptions
  %%> - at most one package group: every eligible major and advisory fix together
  %%> - skipped with the registry check when no file changed and no check was due
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the update targets, the blocked findings and the group request, in the step's output
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - no `orbit-gateway` behavior and no Gateway call
  %%> - no begin or finish note: Swamp records each run, and the Gateway reads the terminal result
  alt run succeeds
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · findings
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Store the inspection<br/>SHAs · packages · findings
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the blob SHAs, the package list and the findings stored for Project 4
    %%> - without `--open`: nothing is created; the result shows the findings
    %%> - task #5150 succeeds
    opt --open, updates eligible
      Note over GW: Open the update group<br/>task group #812 · tasks.provision
      %%> Result:
      %%> - task group #812 with one package group, for one pull request
      %%> - the Gateway admits `tasks.provision` for it; Pi turns then run in its task VM (driver `pi`)
      %%> Not admitted:
      %%> - a group while Project 4 has an open maintenance task group or unfinished work, from the Gateway's own records
    end
  else a step fails
    GH--xSW: token refused or error
    %%> When:
    %%> - the token is refused, a read fails, or a registry does not answer
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code, for example `project.scan_failed`
    Note over GW: Keep the last inspection<br/>task failed · rerun is safe
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5150 fails; the stored SHAs and package list stay, and no task group is created
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the command again with a new key, or wait for the next hourly Schedule fire
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5150
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the counts of targets and blocked findings and any opened group ID once the task has ended
  end
